s the kingside, and if they ignore it, Black can double pressure with Qe7 or Bc5.\n\nReason:  \n**N: f6-e4** maximizes piece activity, central control, and creates immediate tactical threats against White’s center and king. It limits White’s options and increases Black’s initiative.\n\nAnswer: N: f6-e4"}
